            <ArticleTitle>[The effect of different types of weather on external respiratory function in children ill with bronchial asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Questioning of 70 children with bronchial asthma aged 9 to 14 has identified high percent (71.4%) of meteolabile patients who respond to unfavourable weather with changed function of the external respiration. Reduction of pulmonary ventilation led to clinical deterioration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
